-- title:
--   Adic Galois representation from an eigenplane with toric lines
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, a nonzero natural number $N$ and a set $S$ of natural numbers. Let $\mathcal{O}'$ be a complete discrete valuation domain of characteristic zero with finite residue field, with $p$ lying in its maximal ideal, let $K$ be a fraction field of $\mathcal{O}'$, and let $M$ be a finite free $\mathcal{O}'$-module carrying a monoid homomorphism $\rho_M$ from $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ (realised as the $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra automorphisms of `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`) to $\mathrm{End}_{\mathcal{O}'}M$ and a ring homomorphism $T_M$ from the abstract Hecke algebra $\mathbb{Z}[X_\ell : \ell \text{ prime}]$ to $\mathrm{End}_{\mathcal{O}'}M$; let $\chi$ be a ring homomorphism to $\mathcal{O}'$ from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18), the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}}$ of weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \notin S$ and $U_q$ for primes $q \mid N$, $q \notin S$. Assume: (i) there is a $K$-subspace $W \subseteq K \otimes_{\mathcal{O}'} M$ of dimension $2$, stable under the base-changed operators $\rho_M(\sigma)$, on which $T_M(X_\ell)$ acts by the scalar $\chi(T_\ell)$ for every prime $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S$, such that for every such $\ell$, every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ in which $\ell$ is a nonunit and every $\sigma$ lying in the decomposition subgroup of $A$ and inducing $x \mapsto x^{\ell}$ on the residue field of $A$, the trace of $\rho_M(\sigma)$ on $W$ is $\chi(T_\ell)$, and such that for every prime $q \neq p$ with $q \mid N$, $q^2 \nmid N$ and every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ in which $q$ is a nonunit there are a line $L \leq W$ and $a \in K$ with $a^2 = 1$ such that every Frobenius element $\sigma$ at $(A,q)$ acts on $L$ by the scalar $aq$ and satisfies $\rho_M(\sigma)w - aw \in L$ for all $w \in W$; (ii) the Eichler–Shimura relation $\rho_M(\sigma)^2 m - T_M(X_\ell)\rho_M(\sigma)m + \ell\, m = 0$ holds on all of $M$ for Frobenius elements $\sigma$ at such $\ell$; (iii) for every prime $q \nmid N$ with $q \neq p$ and every valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ in which $q$ is a nonunit, the image in $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ of the corresponding inertia subgroup acts trivially on $M$; (iv) the action $\rho_M$ is adically continuous, that is, for each $n$ there is a finite extension $L/\mathbb{Q}$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ such that $\rho_M(\sigma)v - v \in \mathfrak{m}^n M$ for all $v \in M$ and all $\sigma$ fixing $L$ pointwise. Then there exists a rank-two free $\mathcal{O}'$-module with an adically continuous Galois action, an element $\rho$ of [`GaloisRepAdic 𝒪'`](def/GaloisRep_Adic.html#L16), such that: the characteristic polynomial of $\rho(\sigma)$ is $X^2 - \chi(T_\ell)X + \ell$ for every Frobenius element $\sigma$ at every prime $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \notin S$ and every valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ over $\ell$; $\rho$ is unramified at every prime $q \nmid N$ with $q \neq p$, in the sense that the image of every such inertia subgroup acts by the identity; and for every prime $q \neq p$ with $q \mid N$, $q^2 \nmid N$, every valuation subring over $q$ and every Frobenius element $\sigma$ there, the characteristic polynomial of $\rho(\sigma)$ equals $X^2 - (q+1)X + q$ or $X^2 + (q+1)X + q$.
--
--   This is the lattice-and-characteristic-polynomial step in the construction of the two-dimensional $\lambda$-adic representation attached to a weight-two eigenform: an eigenplane in $K \otimes M$ equipped with Eichler–Shimura data and, at the primes exactly dividing the level, with a toric line and a sign, is converted into an adic Galois representation with the Eichler–Shimura characteristic polynomial at the good primes and the special (Steinberg) shape $X^2 \mp (q+1)X + q$ at the primes exactly dividing the level. It is used in the construction of the representation attached to a newform, via [`CuspForm.IsNewform.exists_galoisRepAdic_charpoly_frobenius_eq_of_dvd_of_not_sq_dvd`](thm.html#CuspForm.IsNewform.exists_galoisRepAdic_charpoly_frobenius_eq_of_dvd_of_not_sq_dvd).
